course: dictionary
lesson: 8596
title: Scorer and the -er word
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A scorer is a person who scores. Scorer comes from the verb score, and the ending -er often means someone who does the action. A teacher teaches, a runner runs, and a scorer scores.
explain: In football or netball, the scorer is the player who puts the ball in the goal or wins the points. «Jake and Connor both want to be top scorer» means both of them want the most goals or points. Top scorer is a phrase for the one with the highest number.
explain: In cricket, a scorer is someone different: they sit and keep the score, writing down every run. The same word can name a player or a person who counts. Read the sentence to see which one it means.
explain: «Goal-scorer» joins two words to make one name, a bit like the old Viking and Anglo-Saxon kennings. A kenning names a thing with two-word phrases, such as «ball-kicker». Once you spot the pattern, you can work out new compound words.
fact: Scorer means a player who scores a goal or points.
fact: Scorer can also mean a person who keeps the score, especially in cricket.
fact: «Top scorer» means the player or pupil with the most points or goals.
fact: The -er ending often shows a person who does the action: a scorer scores, a kicker kicks.
fact: A kenning names a thing with two words, such as «goal-scorer» or «ball-kicker».
exercise: «Jake and Connor both want to be top scorer.» What does top scorer mean? | The last player to finish the race | *The player with the most goals or points | The person who keeps the score for the team
exercise: In cricket, the scorer sits and writes down every run. What does scorer mean here? | An umpire who makes the decisions | A player who hits the ball | *A person who keeps the score
exercise: The -er ending means someone who does the action. Which word means a person who teaches? | *teacher | teaching | teach | taught
test: A kenning like «goal-scorer» joins two words to name one thing. What kind of word is scorer in that phrase? | An adjective | A verb | *A noun
test: Which phrase means the pupil with the most points? | a score card | *top scorer | Connor's ankles | a scorer who is late
exam: «The official scorer checked the board after every goal.» What is an official scorer? | A player who runs fastest | *A person who keeps the record of the score | A goalkeeper who stops the shots | A coach who picks the team
